venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
chroma_db/
*.db

# Raw per-ticket sweep output and archived old sweeps are bulky and
# regenerable -- ignore them, but report.md/report.json (written by Part B)
# are the committed history of eval results over the project's life, so
# explicitly un-ignore those two even though they live under eval/results/.
# eval/results/adversarial/*.json
# Paired A/B trigger-experiment output -- same class as the raw sweep output
# above: bulky, regenerable, and currently PARTIAL (interrupted mid-run).
eval/results/variance_triggers/
 is the same class of artifact: raw
# per-ticket adversarial sweep output, regenerable by re-running the
# adversarial sweep. Its verdict and undelivered evidence are already
# preserved in the committed report.json/report.md, so the raw per-ticket
# files themselves don't need to be tracked either.
eval/results/raw/*.json
eval/results/adversarial/*.json
eval/results/runs/
!eval/results/report.md
!eval/results/report.json

# transient sweep logs
.sweep*.log
venv-ragas/

# local SSH keys -- never commit
key
key.pub
.judge-*.log
.mood.log

# transient RAGAS resume checkpoints
eval/results/.ragas_checkpoint_*.jsonl
eval/results/.ckpt_*.jsonl
